  "atmosSubject": "weatherx-hq/atmos master merge of PR #501 (GFS point tail reads all 88 leads per field in one banded pass), 2026-10-07, on top of PR #492 (commercial API). Moving from 8a1eef9cfded33df44738c4e45f16b1f597008af spans 247 commits / 3375 files (two first-parent merges: #492 then #501); 2370 of them are docs/, 834 platform/, 34 clients/. PR #501 changes only data/fetch.py and data/test_fetch_gfs_parallel.py: the GFS point-tail Zarr read takes all 88 leads of a field in one banded pass (GFS_TAIL_BAND_BYTES = 64 MiB per band; a single row over budget raises ValueError so the collector goes red instead of abstaining) instead of one read per lead, with synthetic Zarr v3 stores comparing the banded and per-lead reads bit for bit. Measured cause: since 2026-10-06 the whole bake's GFS collector hit its 60-minute timeout on the per-lead tail reads, which skipped every whole-data release. Under data/, ops/ and requirements* 114 files changed: the 2 above plus 112 from PR #492 in data/build_commercial_*, data/commercial_ifs_*, data/verify_commercial_ifs_* (and tests), ops/commercial/**, ops/fusion/**, ops/provider-exit-historical-allowlist.txt, ops/release/test-guard-pages-deploy.mjs, ops/test_ci_efficiency.py and ops/test_core_model_artifact.py; none is imported or run by ops/bake-weatherx.sh, ops/bake-observation-points.sh, ops/weather-lab-ready.sh, ops/platform/* or any workflow that reads this declaration (checked with git grep). The five observation producers, data/observation_freshness.py, data/requirements.txt, data/requirements.lock, ops/core_model_artifact.py, ops/platform/publish-r2-component.sh, ops/bake-weatherx.sh, ops/bake-observation-points.sh, ops/weather-lab-ready.sh and the cycle-side five-feed contract are byte-identical. Outside data/ and ops/, 1 app/ file changed (app/functions/_commercialFusionEngine.ts, PR #492); app/package.json and app/package-lock.json are unchanged, so the whole bake's npm ci --prefix app installs the same tree. platform/edge (package.json and lockfile included) changed but is used only by workflows that pin their own Atmos commits. Atmos CI (ci run 37685266508, quality run 37685266671) was still running at this SHA when the pin moved; a passing whole bake at this pin is unverified until one runs.",
